  "_why": "The fixture has silently lost a block three times. Twice a markdown edit matched nothing and did nothing, and the build stayed green because a missing block looks exactly like a block that was never asked for. Only an unrelated count caught the last one. These are EXACT counts, not minimums, so a fixture that loses a block fails loudly and so does one that gains a duplicate.",
  "_updating": "Changing the fixture means changing this file in the same commit. That is the point: the count becomes a deliberate statement rather than whatever happened to render.",
